  "description": "Our clients (owners of 8 Lionel Gardens) wish to build a high quality contemporary 1 bedroom home on the adjacent plot (8a Lionel Gardens) as a build-to-rent property.\n\nThrough an analysis of the local character and context we have developed a design which enhances the character of the area, using high quality materials which are low in embodied energy. We are also in the process of developing the energy strategy for the home to ensure that it exceeds Part L of the building regulations in terms of energy consumption in use. The home has been designed to meet part M4(2) of the building regulations and the design standards described in the London Plan 2021. \n\nThe house will be a low carbon contemporary addition to Lionel Gardens and its purposefully subordinate to the existing terrace. The top line of the elevation has been set back so as to not extend above the eaves height of the No.8 with an inset upstand containing the green roof. \n\nThe front elevation has two large windows only, with an angled porch at the ground floor to create a sheltered area adjacent to the door, with a short entrance ramp to allow the ground floor level to be set slightly lower than the adjacent house. \n\nThe building is monolithic in it's form and appearance and is predominately finished in pigmented lime render, coloured using red oxide which will give a deep red tone to the building. \n\nThe glazing frames, door and upstands will be a close match to this although will be a solid colour without any variation in tone (lime plaster will have some subtle variations in tone). ",
